WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.234
-Welcome back to our show.
-I'm happy to be here.

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:05.200
-Thanks for always coming on.
You know we love you here.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.601
Man, you're phenomenal in
"The Batman."

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:08.434
-Thank you.
-You were unbelievable.

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:10.200
I can't wait to get in
and talk to you about that.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.634
I'm just so happy.
I'm like, "Go, Zoe! Go!"

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:15.400
You just crush it.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.734
But I also -- It's a big --
That's this weekend.

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:18.767
It's going to be
the biggest movie.

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:20.167
I'm so excited about it.

00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:22.467
Then, next weekend, you're
hosting "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:23.467
-Uh-huh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:25.234
♪♪

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:27.367
-Why are you -- Why would you

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:28.501
put this much pressure
on yourself?

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:29.601
-I don't know.

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:31.133
This was a
horrible, horrible plan.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:33.067
-Yeah, because then you can only
enjoy that for a week,

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:34.834
because you've got to get right
into -- It's a lot work.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.767
-I'm so scared and so excited.

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:39.868
I keep on asking, like,
friends of mine who have hosted.

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:42.467
I'm asking for
some comfort or something.

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:44.000
-Yes.
-And I tell them I'm scared.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.400
And they all say,
"You should be scared."

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.934
-Oh, my God. No, no, no.

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:48.467
-Not one person
has said like, "Just relax.

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:49.868
You're going to be fine."

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:52.801
-Oh. I'm going to tell you right
now, you're going to be so fine.

00:00:52.801 --> 00:00:53.934
You're awesome. You got this.

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:55.133
-Will you come do
a skit with me?

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:56.367
-Yeah, of course.
I would do anything with you.

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:57.467
Yeah.
-Really?

00:00:57.467 --> 00:01:00.100
-I would do anything
you want me to do.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.200
You don't have to ask twice.
-Okay.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.400
-You kidding me?

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.701
-Put you on the
spot in front of everybody.

00:01:03.701 --> 00:01:05.601
-The stuff that we've done on
our show together, yeah,

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:06.968
the least thing I can do is
do you one favor.

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:08.100
Yeah.
-That would be amazing.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.300
-If you ever need --
But I'm telling you,

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.601
you're going to be set.

00:01:10.601 --> 00:01:12.701
You don't need me.
You have -- It's the best cast.

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:14.734
They have the
best writers, producers.

00:01:14.734 --> 00:01:15.901
You're in good hands.

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:17.901
-I'm just scared I'll,
like, slip or something.

00:01:17.901 --> 00:01:22.334
-No! On live TV?
That would never happen.

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:27.167
Oh, my God.
I think you're going to nail it.

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:28.701
I think you're just a natural.

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:31.801
Every time you come on the show,
you just steal the whole show.

00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:32.801
We all love you.
-Aww, you're very sweet.

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:34.133
-But you really --
But you are --

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:36.734
Honestly, this thing just
kind of went around recently.

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:38.767
It's footage that --

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:40.534
-Oh, boy.
-Yeah, it's -- No, it's great.

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:41.567
-It's cute.
-It's cute.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:42.834
-Okay.
-It's you as a child.

00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:44.067
-Being a ham.

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:45.234
-Yeah, but you were being --
Where were you at?

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:46.634
At a VH1 thing or something?

00:01:46.634 --> 00:01:49.767
-Yeah, my dad, I think,
was doing an interview for VH1,

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:50.934
and I think he went to
the bathroom,

00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:53.701
and then I was like,
"It's my turn!"

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:55.934
-And you were 7 years old.
-Something like that.

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:58.868
-And they were like,
"Hey, while your dad's away --"

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:00.234
-They're like,
"Who is this child?"

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:02.534
-Yeah, they're like,
"Can you sing something?"

00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:04.100
And you just hopped up,
and you're like,

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:06.400
"I'm going to do 'No Scrubs.'"

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:10.934
This is real. Check this out.
Here's baby Zoe Kravitz.

00:02:10.934 --> 00:02:12.801
-♪ I don't want no scrubs ♪

00:02:12.801 --> 00:02:15.868
♪ A scrub
is...get no love from me ♪

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:19.000
♪ Sittin' on the passenger side
of his best friend's ride ♪

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.067
♪ Trying to holler at me ♪

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:22.801
-Yeah!

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:30.267
-"Am I on TV?"
-"Am I on TV?"

00:02:30.267 --> 00:02:32.100
-Why am I wearing a tiara?

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.467
-Yeah, why were you wearing --
-I don't know.

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:35.601
-Because you're just a cute --
"Am I on TV?"

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:38.968
-"Am I on TV?"
-The cutest kid ever. Come on.

00:02:38.968 --> 00:02:41.300
Let's talk about "The Batman,"
because last time, I think,

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.367
you were here,
you were filming, and --

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:44.634
You were in
the middle of filming.

00:02:44.634 --> 00:02:45.868
You can't say anything,
obviously, no spoilers.

00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:46.934
-Yep.

00:02:46.934 --> 00:02:49.334
-But this is two years
in the making.

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:52.901
-Yeah, I got the job in 2019.
-Wowzers.

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:55.667
-And then we got down for
six months because of COVID.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:57.767
And, yeah,
it's been a long journey.

00:02:57.767 --> 00:02:59.234
-Yeah.
-It's been wild.

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:03.334
-And did you know that you were
going to be up for Catwoman?

00:03:03.334 --> 00:03:04.434
Did you --
How did this come about?

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:05.801
-No.

00:03:05.801 --> 00:03:07.234
-Did you push for it and you're
like, "I got to do this"?

00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:09.701
-No. I got a phone call.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:12.200
My agent told me that
I was on the list of actors

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.467
they were looking at.

00:03:13.467 --> 00:03:14.934
And even that
would have been enough.

00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:16.667
To be on that list
was pretty wild.

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:18.767
And then I flew out
to L.A. to meet

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:21.000
Matt Reeves, the director,
and loved him

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.100
and just loved his vision.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.234
-How is he?

00:03:23.234 --> 00:03:25.667
-He's a wonderful human,
wonderful director,

00:03:25.667 --> 00:03:26.667
cares so much.

00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:28.667
He wrote the script, as well.

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:31.267
So, I was just --
I just wanted to work with him.

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:32.767
-And did you know
Robert Pattinson before?

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:34.033
-I knew Rob.

00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:36.033
I knew Rob just from --
I don't know -- around.

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:38.334
-Been around? Yeah.
-Yeah, around.

00:03:38.334 --> 00:03:41.067
-But had never worked with him.
And I'm a huge fan of his work.

00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:45.033
And I had to camera-test with
him, and that was kind of funny.

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:47.400
Just to camera-test
with someone you know

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.133
dressed up as Batman, and you
haven't seen them a while --

00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:51.467
-He was dressed as Batman?

00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:54.667
-Yeah, they put him in, I think,
George Clooney's suit.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.000
But then you kind of catch up.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.968
You know, you're like,
"So, how you been, you know?"

00:03:58.968 --> 00:04:00.534
-He's like, "I'm alright.
Yeah, yeah. No, yeah.

00:04:00.534 --> 00:04:01.634
-"I'm Batman."

00:04:01.634 --> 00:04:02.634
-"Oh, yeah,
I'm Batman, I guess."

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:04.200
Yeah, yeah."
It's wild.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.734
But -- Wait.
So, you do the screen test.

00:04:05.734 --> 00:04:06.901
You walk in,
he's dressed as Batman?

00:04:06.901 --> 00:04:09.033
-Yeah. Only from the waist up,
by the way.

00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:12.100
He was wearing sweatpants
at the bottom.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.667
-Oh, my God!

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:15.634
You've seen something no one's
ever seen --

00:04:15.634 --> 00:04:16.801
Batman wearing sweatpants.

00:04:16.801 --> 00:04:17.968
-Like, casual Batman.

00:04:17.968 --> 00:04:20.701
-Casual Batman.
That's in the sequel.

00:04:20.701 --> 00:04:22.300
-Yeah, for sure.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.067
-Wait. So, you go in, you go,
"Oh, my gosh."

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:26.334
That's -- I mean,
that's acting right there.

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:27.567
I mean, you got to go in there,
and you're like,

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:28.901
"Hey, let's just go for it,

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.501
because I know you,
and now you're Batman."

00:04:30.501 --> 00:04:32.167
-Like, he was so good that
I actually --

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:34.167
I was so scared that I was
gonna just be thinking like,

00:04:34.167 --> 00:04:35.367
"Oh, my God.
It's Rob dressed as Batman.

00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:36.801
That's weird."
-Yeah.

00:04:36.801 --> 00:04:39.534
-But he was so wonderful that
I totally forgot it was him,

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:41.200
actually,
which was really impressive.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.300
-Yeah, he, honestly, is amazing.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:44.734
But you're amazing,
as well, in this.

00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:45.868
It just all works.

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:47.701
And I --
You just go into this world

00:04:47.701 --> 00:04:50.467
and you forget who --
That you know anyone.

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:51.834
I'm like, "Oh, these are just
great actors in this."

00:04:51.834 --> 00:04:53.834
-Oh, I'm so happy to hear that.
-Oh, I loved it.

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:57.567
And I was like, "Okay, now, if I
was cast as Catwoman --"

00:04:57.567 --> 00:04:59.067
-Which you might --
Which you still might be.

00:04:59.067 --> 00:05:00.467
-I was on the list.
-You're still young, Jimmy.

00:05:00.467 --> 00:05:02.934
-My agent called me, as well.
I know. I was so nervous.

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:04.067
I was like, "Oh, my God.

00:05:04.067 --> 00:05:05.367
Don't get me
in the room with Rob."

00:05:05.367 --> 00:05:06.534
Oh, my God.

00:05:06.534 --> 00:05:09.267
"Because I'm wearing
sweatpants, as well."

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:11.934
But I would
study -- I would study cats.

00:05:11.934 --> 00:05:12.968
-I did that.

00:05:12.968 --> 00:05:16.234
-I would drink milk
out of a bowl.

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:17.934
-I did that.
-You did not.

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:19.701
-I did.
-You drank milk out of a bowl?

00:05:19.701 --> 00:05:21.567
-Maybe.

00:05:21.567 --> 00:05:23.601
I'm method, dude.
-Me too, man.

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:25.334
Dude, I'm so into --
You don't --

00:05:25.334 --> 00:05:27.033
Well, I mean, no spoilers.
Yeah, anyways...

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:29.067
-I hung out with cats.
-Yeah.

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:30.234
-A lot.

00:05:30.234 --> 00:05:32.868
-See, that's where I'm --
As I'm thinking now,

00:05:32.868 --> 00:05:34.701
I think I'm allergic to cats.

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.300
-Which is why --
Which is the only reason

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:37.434
you didn't get this part.

00:05:37.434 --> 00:05:38.467
-Thank you.
-Yeah.

00:05:38.467 --> 00:05:40.167
-And that's like --
But then also

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:43.100
more of a challenge for
the role for me.

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:45.968
But I would be like -- I do like
cats because they're curious.

00:05:45.968 --> 00:05:47.667
I find them interesting.

00:05:47.667 --> 00:05:49.901
I feel like they
could kill me any two seconds.

00:05:49.901 --> 00:05:51.133
-I was really inspired by that.

00:05:51.133 --> 00:05:54.100
I watched a bunch of cat videos,
feline videos,

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:55.567
watching them fight.

00:05:55.567 --> 00:05:58.901
And what I was so interested by
was the fact that you can --

00:05:58.901 --> 00:06:00.767
You can't read
their face at all,

00:06:00.767 --> 00:06:04.133
which is why I think people
are kind of creeped out by them.

00:06:04.133 --> 00:06:05.367
But you can't tell
what they're going to do.

00:06:05.367 --> 00:06:07.267
-They go, "Oh, my gosh.
Kitty loves me."

00:06:07.267 --> 00:06:08.367
-Yeah, Then, all of a sudden,

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:09.400
the kitty scratches
your face out.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:10.634
-Kitty scratches
your face out, yeah,

00:06:10.634 --> 00:06:13.334
and be like, "Get off,"
like, and then leaves.

00:06:13.334 --> 00:06:14.634
-Yeah. They don't care.
-No, they don't --

00:06:14.634 --> 00:06:16.100
-They don't care.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:17.968
They were the hardest thing
to control during the shooting.

00:06:17.968 --> 00:06:19.200
We were doing,
like, crazy stunts,

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:20.601
and, like, all that was fine.

00:06:20.601 --> 00:06:24.200
But then, like, getting a cat to
stay in one place -- impossible.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:25.968
Impossible.
-There's no actor cats.

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:29.968
-No. We -- I -- They tried to
get me to "know the cats"

00:06:29.968 --> 00:06:31.167
that were Selina's cats.

00:06:31.167 --> 00:06:32.367
And it's funny.

00:06:32.367 --> 00:06:33.868
They would say, you know,
"Training at 1:30

00:06:33.868 --> 00:06:36.033
and then rehearsal at this time
and then cat time."

00:06:36.033 --> 00:06:37.934
And I was like,
"What's cat time?"

00:06:37.934 --> 00:06:42.133
And it was just putting me in
a room with a bunch of cats,

00:06:42.133 --> 00:06:44.667
with the cats that
were going to be my cats.

00:06:44.667 --> 00:06:46.033
-Thinking that it might help.

00:06:46.033 --> 00:06:48.300
-But the cats didn't care.
-No, they're cats.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:49.367
-I was just sitting here,

00:06:49.367 --> 00:06:50.734
and the cats
would just walk away.

00:06:50.734 --> 00:06:52.000
It did nothing.
It did nothing for --

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:53.167
-They did -- Well,
they did great in the movie.

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:55.367
If the cats are watching,
you did a great job.

00:06:55.367 --> 00:06:57.968
-You guys are amazing.

00:06:57.968 --> 00:06:59.234
-When we come back,

00:06:59.234 --> 00:07:00.801
I want to show a clip from
"The Batman."

00:07:00.801 --> 00:07:02.968
More with Zoe Kravitz after
the break, everybody.

